this is a collection of bugs that i consider "fairly minor", as in
worth fixing since their kind've annoying. 

i'm sorry, but i don't know whether any of these have been mentioned before or
not (since i haven't been very good about reading rec.games.nethack).

this is nethack 3.0 patch level 7, on a 386 PC running AT&T SVR3.2

1) naming a class of objects "#name, n, X" results in "a rusty pot"
	becoming "a helmet called helmet".

2) sometimes the final "print posessions" display fails to show
	the identified posessions, but instead displays them with the
	same characteristics the player already know.  this appears
	to be related to hitting ^c (SIGINT) before the display commences

